# hermes-telegram-ads

Production-ready Python adapter for **ads.telegram.org** — designed for the Hermes Agent.
Built on Playwright with a wrapped JSON internal API, Pydantic types, and a safety layer
that prevents mutating actions without explicit user confirmation.

Derived from a 7-phase reverse-engineering of the site (see
`docs/site_maps/telegram_ads/FULL_SITE_MAP.md` if available).

## Status

- ✅ **121/121 unit tests passing**
- ✅ Full API coverage: 14 internal `/api?hash=<csrf>` methods + 1 multipart `/file/upload`
- ✅ Both **TON** (Personal / Channel / Organization) and **Stars** (Bot Account) cabinets
- ✅ Schedule encoding (Phase 5 verified), search-query base64 encoding (Phase 6 verified)
- ✅ Two-step destructive operations with `confirm_hash`
- ✅ Safety layer with risk levels + Confirmation tokens
- ✅ Audit log (JSONL, token hashing)
- ⚠ Browser tool not auto-tested (requires live Telegram login session)

## Install

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
python -m playwright install chromium
```

## Quick start

```python
import asyncio
from hermes_telegram_ads import TelegramAdsAdapter, TelegramAdsConfig

async def main():
    config = TelegramAdsConfig.from_yaml("config.yaml")  # or .default()
    async with TelegramAdsAdapter.start(config) as ads:
        await ads.ensure_logged_in()                      # raises if not logged in
        accounts = await ads.list_accounts()
        await ads.choose_account(accounts[0].account_token)
        ads_list = await ads.list_ads()
        for a in ads_list[:5]:
            print(a.ad_id, a.title, a.status, a.spent, "/", a.budget)

asyncio.run(main())
```

## Architecture

```
hermes_telegram_ads/
├── adapter.py           ← TelegramAdsAdapter (public facade)
├── api.py               ← TelegramAdsApi (POST /api?hash=<csrf>)
├── browser.py           ← BrowserAutomationTool (Playwright wrapper)
├── safety.py            ← Risk levels + Confirmation tokens
├── audit.py             ← JSONL audit log
├── config.py            ← Pydantic config (load from YAML)
├── constants.py         ← URLs, method names, hard limits
├── types.py             ← Pydantic models (Ad, Account, Event, ...)
├── errors.py            ← Typed exceptions
├── selectors.yaml       ← CSS selectors with versioning
├── parser.py            ← parse_money, parse_int, extract_*
├── payloads.py          ← schedule encoding, search-query base64, draft → payload
├── media.py             ← multipart /file/upload (aspect-ratio 16:9 hard limit)
├── reports.py           ← CSV download via session cookies
└── pages/
    ├── account.py       ← /account, account-switcher dropdown
    ├── ad_detail.py     ← /account/ad/<id>
    ├── ad_stats.py      ← /account/ad/<id>/stats
    ├── budget.py        ← /account/budget + transactions
    ├── events.py        ← /account/events + pixel snippets
    └── profile.py       ← /account/edit
```

## Public action methods (all on `TelegramAdsAdapter`)

### Read (no confirmation needed)

| Method | Returns |
|---|---|
| `open_dashboard()` | navigates to `/account`, returns URL |
| `ensure_logged_in()` | raises `LoginRequiredError` if not authed |
| `list_accounts()` | `list[Account]` (all cabinets accessible) |
| `get_current_account()` | `Account \| None` |
| `list_ads()` | `list[AdSummary]` (homepage table) |
| `get_ad(ad_id)` | `AdDetail` (Info tab) |
| `get_ad_stats(ad_id)` | `AdStats` (charts + monthly table) |
| `get_account_budget()` | `AccountBudget` (balance + tx history) |
| `get_account_stats()` | account-level Statistics page snapshot |
| `get_profile()` | `ProfileInfo` |
| `list_events()` | `list[Event]` (Stars only) |
| `get_pixel_base_snippet()` | `PixelSnippet \| None` |
| `get_event_setup_snippet(event_id)` | per-event snippet |
| `get_event_log(event_id)` | `EventLog` (last 8h, 100 entries) |
| `get_share_stats_url(ad_id)` | public stats URL |
| `validate_ad(draft)` | `checkAdPost` result (live validation) |

### Draft (no irreversible effect)

| Method | Notes |
|---|---|
| `save_ad_draft(draft)` | saves form draft on server |
| `prepare_ad_draft(draft)` | save + validate + preview screenshot |
| `upload_media(file_path)` | returns media token (16:9 required) |
| `create_similar_draft(source_ad_id)` | clones ad → draft |
| `screenshot(name=None)` | takes screenshot, returns path |

### Mutating (require Confirmation)

All mutating actions return `ConfirmationRequiredError` unless caller passes a
valid `confirmation_id`. Issue confirmation first, surface details to the user,
then call the action with the id.

```python
draft = CreateAdDraft(...)
conf = ads.issue_create_ad_confirmation(draft, note="for user review")
# ↑ Skill/UI surfaces conf details to the human, gets explicit yes.
await ads.create_ad(draft, confirmation_id=conf.id)
```

| Method | Risk | Helper to issue confirmation |
|---|---|---|
| `create_ad(draft, confirmation_id)` | CONFIRM | `issue_create_ad_confirmation(draft)` |
| `edit_ad(EditAdDraft, confirmation_id)` | CONFIRM | `issue_edit_ad_confirmation(draft)` |
| `change_cpm(ad_id, cpm, confirmation_id)` | CONFIRM | `issue_change_cpm_confirmation(ad_id, cpm)` |
| `change_status(ad_id, active, confirmation_id)` | CONFIRM | `issue_change_status_confirmation(ad_id, active=...)` |
| `add_to_budget(ad_id, amount, confirmation_id)` | CONFIRM | `issue_add_budget_confirmation(ad_id, amount)` |
| `withdraw_from_budget(ad_id, amount, confirmation_id)` | CONFIRM | `issue_withdraw_budget_confirmation(ad_id, amount)` |
| `create_event(title, event_type, confirmation_id)` | CONFIRM | `issue_create_event_confirmation(title, event_type)` |

### Mutating + double confirmation

```python
c1, c2 = ads.issue_delete_ad_confirmations(ad_id=11)
await ads.delete_ad(ad_id=11, confirmation_id=c1.id, second_confirmation_id=c2.id)
```

| Method | Helper |
|---|---|
| `delete_ad(ad_id, ...)` | `issue_delete_ad_confirmations(ad_id)` |
| `delete_event(event_id, ...)` | `issue_delete_event_confirmations(event_id)` |
| `revoke_share_stats_url(ad_id, ...)` | `issue_revoke_stats_url_confirmations(ad_id)` |

### Forbidden by default

These require deliberate config opt-in (and are not exposed as methods yet):

- `transferStars` — permanent transfer of bot Stars to ad account
- external Fragment payment initiation
- `createPixel` (first-time pixel creation, untested)
- `editEvent` / `renameEvent` (not in spec)

## Confirmation lifecycle

```
1. Skill builds the action's params.
2. Skill calls `issue_*_confirmation(...)` → gets a Confirmation object.
3. Skill surfaces Confirmation.id, action, params_fingerprint to user.
4. User says yes / no.
5. If yes — pass id back to the action method.
6. Adapter consumes the confirmation atomically (one-shot).
7. Re-using the id, expired (default TTL 5 min), or modifying params
   between issue and consume raises InvalidConfirmationError.
```

## Geo / cabinet rules (hard)

- **TON cabinet** cannot reach users with phone country codes **RU / UA / IL / PS**.
  Calling `safety.check_ton_geo_safe({"RU", ...})` raises `GeoTargetingError`.
- **Stars cabinet** has no such restriction (it's Telegram's internal currency).
- For RU/UA/IL/PS audience — use Stars (Bot Account) cabinet only.
- Stars are NOT bought — they accumulate from your bot's Stars revenue, then
  transferred (permanently) into the ad account.

## Login

Login is **manual**. Telegram requires a confirmation tap inside the Telegram
app — the adapter intentionally has no auto-confirm flow.

First-time setup:
1. Run any example or `ensure_logged_in()`.
2. Browser opens `https://ads.telegram.org`.
3. Enter your phone, confirm in Telegram.
4. Cookies persist in `browser.profile_dir` for future runs.

## Configuration

See [`config.example.yaml`](./config.example.yaml). Load with:

```python
config = TelegramAdsConfig.from_yaml("path/to/config.yaml")
```

Or programmatically:

```python
from hermes_telegram_ads.config import TelegramAdsConfig, BrowserConfig

config = TelegramAdsConfig(browser=BrowserConfig(headless=True))
config.ensure_paths()
```

## Audit log

All actions are logged to JSONL (default `./logs/telegram_ads_audit.jsonl`).
`account_token` is SHA-256 truncated by default (`hash_account_tokens: true`).
Sensitive blobs (`raw_response`, `html`) are excluded.

Example entry:
```json
{
  "time": "2026-05-28T12:00:00+00:00",
  "tool": "telegram_ads",
  "action": "editAdCPM",
  "risk_level": "confirm_required",
  "result_status": "ok",
  "account_token_hash": "sha256:0000000000000000",
  "confirmation_id": "11111111-2222-...",
  "ad_id": 11,
  "cpm": 0.41
}
```

## Internal API spec

```
POST https://ads.telegram.org/api?hash=<csrf>
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Cookie: <session cookie>

owner_id=<account_token>&<params>&method=<methodName>
```

| Method | Wrapper | Returns |
|---|---|---|
| `searchChannel` | `api.search_channel(query, field)` | `{ok, channel}` |
| `checkAdPost` | `api.check_ad_post(payload)` | `{field, error, preview_data}` |
| `createAd` | `api.create_ad(payload)` | `{ok, redirect_to}` |
| `saveAdDraft` | `api.save_ad_draft(payload)` | `{ok}` |
| `createDraftFromAd` | `api.create_draft_from_ad(ad_id)` | `{ok, redirect_to}` |
| `editAd` | `api.edit_ad(payload)` | `{ok, redirect_to}` |
| `editAdCPM` ⚠ uppercase | `api.edit_ad_cpm(ad_id, cpm)` | `{ok, ad}` |
| `editAdStatus` | `api.edit_ad_status(ad_id, active)` | `{ok, ad}` |
| `incrAdBudget` | `api.incr_ad_budget(ad_id, amount)` | `{ok, ad}` |
| `decrAdBudget` ⚠ param `amount` | `api.decr_ad_budget(ad_id, amount)` | `{ok, ad}` |
| `createEvent` | `api.create_event(title, type)` | `{ok, event, ...}` |
| `deleteEvent` (2-step) | `api.delete_event_full(event_id)` | `{ok, redirect_to}` |
| `deleteAd` (2-step) | `api.delete_ad_full(ad_id)` | `{ok, redirect_to}` |
| `revokeStatsUrl` | `api.revoke_stats_url(ad_id)` | `{ok, new_url, toast}` |
| `POST /file/upload` (multipart) | `api.upload_media(file_path)` | `{ok, media}` |

Bootstrap is lazy; auto-re-bootstrap on CSRF rotation. Call
`api.rebootstrap()` explicitly after `choose_account()` (owner_id changes).

## Hard constraints baked into adapter

- Text ≤ 160 chars (raises `PolicyViolationError`)
- Max 1 inline link in text; only `@`/`t.me/` formats
- No URL shorteners, no IP addresses in URL
- `incrAdBudget`: budget after add ≥ 1.00 TON (server-enforced; surfaced as error)
- `decrAdBudget`: 2-minute cooldown after `editAdStatus` toggle
- Media upload: aspect ratio 16:9 (local pre-check + server-enforced)
- Targeting immutable after `createAd` — use `create_similar_draft`
- Conversion Event immutable after first save with it
- Telegram login is manual — adapter will never auto-enter codes

## Testing

```bash
pytest                  # 121 tests, ~0.7s
pytest -k payloads      # schedule encoding + base64 query
pytest -k safety        # confirmation gates + policy checks
```

Tests don't need Playwright/browser — they validate against captured fixtures
in `tests/fixtures/` (real Phase 4-7 API responses and form bodies).

